!! 5. The slices

Each slice: what changes · build · tests red first with CONTROL · anchors. Tests are named so a builder can grep them.

!!! M1. The mirror boots stock in browser mode (A1 + A2 + A3 + A4)

''Why one slice.'' A1 alone (browser mode, no lends) boots a page where `initSavers` constructs `put.js` and probes the network, `trapErrors` claims `window.onerror`, and a person's `syncadaptor` would stand a Syncer. Those are the cures of A2-A4. Shipping A1 without them is a half-state the alpha law refuses.

''Build''
# ''The page boot env.'' Add `makePageBootEnv()` beside `makeBrowserWorkerBootEnv` (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:288`, WT): `preSeedTw = {boot:{suppressBoot:true, disabledStartupModules:[…M1 set…]}, node:null}`; no `processArg`, no `fs`/`vm`, real `window` as the loader's `window` parameter (`:346-354`), `undefined` as its `process` parameter. Do not pre-seed `browser` (F1).
# ''The page branch of `prepareHostBootInstance`'' (`:453-485`): delete the five lends (`:455-473`), the release hold, and the `configureIslandRuntime` call (`:477`). Keep `MIRROR_TOKEN` and `instance.utils.nextTick = queueMicrotask` (`:479`). `bootWithHostBridge` (`:529-575`) lends no `require` on the page path.
# ''The disabled set'' (F2, by name): `story`, `rootwidget`, `render`, `password`, `favicon`, `windows`. ''Not'' `browser-messaging` (changed from spec.md; §2.1). `load-modules`, `info`, `plugins`, `startup`, `confirm`, `eventbus` stand.
# ''The saver shadows'', as tiddlers of the house plugin with `plugin-priority` above `0`: the fifteen `$:/core/modules/savers/*.js` titles with ''no `module-type`'' (F2 confirms the override), `$:/config/SaverFilter` empty, `$:/config/AutoSave` = `no`. `tm-download-file` on the inert `SaverHandler` (`saver-handler.js:103`) stays bound; it finds no `download` saver and does nothing, so the house door (M2) is the one that acts.
# ''`lar-story`'' (house startup module): `openStartupTiddlers` and `tm-home` only; `print`, `open-external` as `lar:service` kinds; `tm-browser-refresh` as a `route` reload under the unload hold; permalink/permaview as `route` writes (M2's route door).
# ''The window-claim dispositions'' (F5): snapshot `window.onerror` before eval and restore after, `$tw.boot.tasks.trapErrors=false` after `bootprefix` runs (set it on the instance after eval, before `boot.boot`); `lendAlertRailError(tw)` extracted from `configureIslandRuntime` (`:424-431`) and assigned before `boot.boot`; restore `window.onbeforeunload` after boot; detach `$tw.passwordPrompt.promptWrapper` and replace `$tw.passwordPrompt` with a stub that raises `refused/password`; `delete window.sjcl` after `boot.boot` (safe: F5); keep `window.$tw` while mounted, remove at unmount.
# ''The census before boot'': `censusPreloads(preloads)` in `glass-mirror.ts` before `TW5Engine.boot` (`:45`): parse each plugin's JSON, count shadows whose `module-type` reads `syncadaptor` or `saver`; drop the plugin, raise `$:/temp/lares/alert/refused/plugin-syncadaptor/<title>` through the port's alert road, write `refused-plugin:<n>` into `data-lar-mirror`. Belt after boot: `$tw.syncer === undefined && $tw.syncadaptor === undefined`, else teardown `syncer-stood`.

''Tests (red first, each with its control)''
* `mirror-boots-browser-mode` (vitest-browser or Playwright, Chromium + Firefox): after `openMirror`, `$tw.browser` truthy, `$tw.node === null`. ''Control:'' the island boot in a Worker still reads `browser === null && node === null`.
* `mirror-leaves-no-lends`: `['Buffer','global','process','setImmediate','clearImmediate'].every(n => !(n in window))` while mounted. ''Control:'' the pre-boot snapshot of those five names equals the post-boot one.
* `mirror-process-hazard-closed`: define `globalThis.process = {}` before boot; `$tw.node === null`. ''Control:'' a test-only env without `node:null` reads `$tw.node` as `{}`.
* `mirror-boot-makes-no-request` (Playwright over `http://127.0.0.1`): zero OPTIONS/HEAD from boot to first paint. ''Control:'' a stock TW5 HTML of `ea94ca840` served the same way makes them.
* `mirror-disabled-set-holds`: `$tw.boot.disabledStartupModules` equals the named set; `$tw.titlePublisher` undefined. ''Control:'' stock defines it.
* `mirror-saver-handler-inert`: edit 10 tiddlers; no `tc-dirty` on `document.body`; `$tw.unloadTasks.every(t => !t({}))`. ''Control:'' with the house plugin's three config tiddlers removed, `tc-dirty` lands.
* `mirror-saver-shadows-win`: `$tw.wiki.getShadowSource("$:/core/modules/savers/put.js")` names the house plugin, and `$tw.modules.types.saver` holds no `put.js`. ''Control:'' with the house plugin's priority set to `0` and a title sorting before `$:/core`, core's shadow wins and `put.js` is defined (F2's tiebreak).
* `mirror-refuses-syncadaptor-plugin-by-name` / `mirror-refuses-saver-plugin-by-name`: fixture plugin with a `module-type: syncadaptor` (resp. `saver`) shadow; alert names it; `$tw.syncer` undefined; the mirror paints. ''Control:'' the same plugin with `module-type: library` loads with no alert.
* `mirror-window-claims-dispositioned`: `window.onerror`, `window.onbeforeunload`, `'sjcl' in window` equal their pre-boot snapshot; `document.body` gains no engine child; `#storeArea` absent. ''Control:'' stock shows all four claims.
* `mirror-fault-reaches-alert-rail`: a fixture plugin throws in a startup module; `boot-fault/N` alert lands; no `.tc-error-form` in `document.body`. ''Control:'' stock paints the form.

''Anchors.'' WT `tw5-host-bridge.ts:167-175,195,226-247,288-306,346-356,393-431,453-485,529-575`; `glass-mirror.ts:45`; `tw5-vm.ts:40,54,63,65`; `page-mirror.ts:32-35`; `glass-port-adaptor.ts:37,72-74`; TW5 F1, F2, F4, F5.

!!! M2. The camera under `$tw.rootWidget`, `lar-root-services` in browser mode, and the route door (A5 + A6 + A7)

''Build''
# ''Camera'' (`glass-camera.ts`, WT): drop the minted root (`:33-34`) and the `browser`/`pageScroller`/`popup` lends (`:40-49`); `load-modules` built `$tw.rootWidget`, `startup` built `$tw.popup`, M2 builds `$tw.pageScroller`. Render `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate` with `parentWidget: $tw.rootWidget` into the shadow container; set `$tw.pageWidgetNode`, `$tw.pageContainer = container`, `$tw.styleWidgetNode`, `$tw.styleElement = shadowStyle`; run `render.js:115-116`'s `domNodes`/`children` fix-up; emit `th-page-refreshing`/`th-page-refreshed` around every refresh; the draft throttle off `$:/config/Drafts/TypingTimeout` (default 400) as `render.js:88-113`; `$:/tags/StartupAction/PostRender` once after first paint. Write the line: //timers pace paint, never truth//.
# ''`lar-root-services`'' (M `packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/lar-root-services.ts:94` and its `tiddlers/src/` twin): the guard reads a capability (`$tw.larSurface`, set by the mirror's boot inputs or the island's camera), never `$tw.browser`; the header (`:37`) and the `tm-http-request` comment (`:35`) get rewritten to the door law. Mirror half: `$tw.modal`, `$tw.notifier`, `$tw.pageScroller` as house objects painting into a `<div class="lar-root-layer">` in the shadow root; modals as a shadow-root `<dialog>` opened with `showModal()` (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#dom-dialog-showmodal); `tm-modal`, `tm-show-switcher`, `tm-notify`, and the pure-wiki `tm-rename-tiddler`, `tm-relink-tiddler`, `tm-focus-selector`, `tm-scroll` as `rootwidget.js:81-109`. Door half through `lar:service`: clipboard, download, `open-surface` (`tm-open-window`), print, open-external, fullscreen, route; `http-request` crosses as the D15 door once M3's seam stands, refused by name until then (`:216-218`).
# ''Route door'': stands before any mirror boot; reads the full URL into route state; `history.replaceState` drops any fragment so `initStartup` reads an empty hash (F5); the first `hashchange` listener on `window` calls `stopImmediatePropagation()`; `#:safe` burns; `document.title` belongs to the route door, fed by the camera's render of `$:/core/wiki/title` on `$tw.fakeDocument`.

''Tests''
* `camera-emits-page-refresh-hooks`: a hook-counter module records one `th-page-refreshing` and one `th-page-refreshed` per change batch. ''Control:'' stock records the same counts over the same script.
* `camera-runs-postrender-once`; `camera-draft-throttle` (''Control:'' a non-draft edit refreshes at once).
* `mirror-modal-paints-in-root-layer`: `tm-modal` → `dialog[open]` inside the shadow root; `document.body` gains nothing. ''Control:'' the island camera's `tm-modal` still writes the frame hint.
* `mirror-no-root-double-handler`: `$tw.rootWidget.eventListeners["tm-http-request"]` has exactly one handler, and likewise `tm-modal`, `tm-notify`, `tm-print`, `tm-open-window` (F3 is why this test exists).
* `mirror-http-request-refused-by-name` (until M3): no request; alert `refused/http-request`. ''Control:'' stock fires it.
* `mirror-services-doors`: golden 12 at full; copy and download `applied`, print refused.
* `route-door-burns-safe-hash`: `…/#:safe` → `$tw.safeMode` falsy, no fragment. ''Control:'' stock reads `true`.
* `route-door-owns-hashchange`: `location.hash = "#Foo"` opens nothing. ''Control:'' stock opens `Foo`.
* `mirror-story-never-writes-hash`: ten navigations leave `location.hash` empty.

''Anchors.'' WT `glass-camera.ts:9-13,33-34,40-49,57-66`; M `lar-root-services.ts:35,37,80,94,107,119,216-218`; TW5 F3, F5, F6.

!!! M3. The crossings: the fence, the alert, the library, the door seam (NEW)

''Build'' (§2.1)
# ''The face's crossing list'' as a face intent: `crossings: [{origin, kinds}]` (`project_face_intent_plane`; the intent files are I2's, fenced by the D3 kit, so M3 reads the list through a port verb `face:crossings` the vessel answers, and the //write// of a new crossing rides the existing intent road, not a new store).
# ''The fence'': `standCrossingFence(list, portOrigin)` in `lararium-web/src/glass/` composes the policy and inserts the meta ''before'' `bootGlass` (`stand.ts:3`, step L3) — in L1, beside the shadow root, so the CAS read (L2) itself runs under it. Policy as §2.1.2. The node's page server sends the same policy as a header where it serves the page. The fence governs the page realm alone: the daemon and wiki workers load from same-origin `https:` URLs and take their own policy from their script response (§1b row 28), so the vessel's own reaches (the port's `wss://`, the D15 door, CAS pulls) run under house code, never under the face's page list. `worker-src 'self'` keeps a plugin from spawning a `blob:` worker past the fence.
# ''The alert'': `securitypolicyviolation` → `$:/temp/lares/alert/refused/crossing/<origin>` with `violatedDirective` and `blockedURI`, and an action tiddler that writes the intent. The re-fence takes effect at the next navigation (the clean-realm reload K3 supplies; before K3, a plain reload).
# ''`browser-messaging` stock''; `$:/config/OfficialPluginLibrary` stock.
# ''The `http-request` seam'': `lar-root-services` forwards `tm-http-request` as `lar:service{kind:"http-request"}`; the surface's manifest carries it only when the vessel declares the D15 door; the island side of D15 (allowlist, private-range refusal, sensed snapshot with provenance, recorded-fixture goldens) stays ''D15's row'' in D1, not this lane. M3 lands the seam and the refusal-by-manifest.

''Tests''
* `fence-stands-before-engine`: a `fetch("https://example.invalid/")` from a fixture plugin's startup module rejects with a CSP violation, and the alert names `example.invalid` and `connect-src`. ''Control:'' with `https://example.invalid` on the face list the fetch reaches the network (Playwright route intercept sees it).
* `fence-is-up-before-cas-read`: step L2's CAS read runs under the policy (`document.querySelector('meta[http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"]')` exists at L2). ''Control:'' the island worker boot adds no meta.
* `library-loads-through-allowed-frame`: with `https://tiddlywiki.com` on the `frame` list (Playwright serving a fixture library page at that origin by route), `tm-load-plugin-library` lands `$:/temp/RemoteAssetInfo/…` tiddlers and the port sees the writes. ''Control:'' without the origin, the iframe fails by `frame-src`, no tiddler lands, the alert names it.
* `installed-plugin-waits-for-boot-census`: a library install of a `syncadaptor` plugin lands as tiddlers, and the ''next'' boot's census refuses it by name (M1's test, re-run over an installed plugin).
* `http-request-crosses-as-door`: `tm-http-request` with the door in the manifest posts `lar:service{kind:"http-request"}` and makes no page request; without it, `refused/http-request`. ''Control:'' stock fires XHR.
* `fence-header-and-meta-compose` (node-served page): with the header present and a narrower meta, the narrower wins; with no header, the meta alone fences.

''Anchors.'' WT `glass/stand.ts:35-50`; `glass-mirror.ts:45`; M `lar-root-services.ts:216-218`; TW5 `browser-messaging.js:42-54,100-121,158-196`, `rootwidget.js:31-57`; `dreamdom-roadmap.mem:212` (D15); `dreamdom.mem:343-345,539`; F8.

!!! M4. Witnesses at full (A8 + A9 + goldens + G6 + G7)

Unchanged from spec.md A8, A9 and D, with these corrections:
* The five `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` sites un-skip together once A1 hands the camera the real document; the framed editor's style copy inside a shadow root stays ''UNVERIFIED'' until `mirror-five-sites-walk` runs on WebKit.
* G6 on WebKit runs in <code>mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v&lt;repo's &#64;playwright/test version>-noble</code> (§1 row 12).
* G7 adds: iOS 26 Safari as a tab ''and'' as a Home Screen app (two storage regimes; `open()` returns null in the second, §1 row 7, so any popup path reads unmeasurable there); the K3 clean-realm reload cost (lock → re-asked first paint); WebAuthn inside the Home Screen app (§1 row 7.1, unmeasured).
* `glass-echo-lands-once` re-runs under browser mode; `mirror-boot-writes-nothing`; `mirror-landing-normalised-no-echo` as spec.md A9.
* Goldens' expected deliberate diffs: 12 (doors), 7 (shortcuts on the shadow surface), permalink/route, and now the ''crossing alert'' where a stock fixture fetches.

!!! K1. The passkey slot (pure mesh; from day one)

''Build.'' `lararium-mesh/src/keyslot.ts:49-50`: `PinKind = "passphrase" | "paper" | "passkey"`. A passkey pin wraps the slot share under a KEK derived by HKDF from the 32-byte PRF output (`first`) with the pin's place and kind in `info` (the existing "wrapped share moved to another pin or slot does not open" law, `:28`). The pin record stores the credential id and the PRF salt; it stores no output. One route, one pin (`:19-20`) holds: the same credential twice refuses. Vectors: a fixed PRF output → a known wrapped share; a wrong output → `slot-refused`; the pin beside a passphrase pin on one slot, either route opens.

''Tests''
* `keyslot-passkey-pin-opens` / `keyslot-passkey-wrong-output-refuses` / `keyslot-passkey-beside-passphrase` (vectors, Node). ''Control:'' today's `keyslot.ts` refuses the kind by name (`:9-11` "a declared kind with nothing behind it would be a stub").
* `keyslot-passkey-duplicate-route-refuses`.

''Facts.'' §1 rows 3, 4. The output is deterministic per credential and salt (row 4), which is what makes it a route. A synced passkey reads `cloud-synced` in `vault status` (`secure-context.mem` #/custody-leans, caution 4).

!!! K2. Custody into the worker; signers into the worker; the holder flag burns (B1 + B2 + B3)

As spec.md B1-B3, with these corrections and the compose-hunk note (§3.2):
* The `custody:*` door on the daemon worker (kinds join `island-protocol.ts:705-733` and `holder-routes.ts:6-45`); `browser-custody.ts` and `keyslot`/`tree-key` leave the page bundle's import graph; the manifest drops `atom.seed`, `faceAddressSecret`, `veilArchiveBytes` (`open-browser-vessel.ts:1335-1338` — ''the chain hunk''); per-tab ask; `sign{purpose, bytes}` with a closed purpose set and bytes composed in the worker.
* Device key: reading ''(ii)'' — sealed at rest (`sealed/vessel-key`, `browser-custody.ts:311-323`), imported `extractable:false` into worker memory per unlock (RFC 8410 pkcs8 prefix), seed zeroed. Reading (i) is refused by two measured facts: the handle structured-clones to any realm as a permanent signing oracle, and the seed sits cleartext on disk regardless (`secure-context.mem:133-135`).
* Every page signing site moves (spec.md B2 list, re-anchored); the page bundle holds no <code>&#64;noble/ed25519</code>.
* `?holder` burns (`main.ts:53-62`); the dedicated worker stays; the holder relays ciphertext and store coordination only if it ever returns.
* Tests as spec.md B1-B3 (`custody-key-never-in-page` with its heap-probe control run ''first''; `page-imports-no-custody`; `manifest-carries-no-secret`; `per-tab-ask-holds`; `device-key-opaque-in-worker`; `device-key-no-handle-at-rest`; `page-cannot-sign`; `mirror-plugins-wait-on-seal`; `holder-carries-no-secret`). Safari: verify signatures, never compare bytes (§1 row 6).

''Anchors.'' M `browser-custody.ts:27,60-61,96,99-102,311-323,383,405-408,412,437,482,511-535,552,565,574-587,645-687`; `browser-vessel-identity.ts:77-82,183-191,216-227`; `open-browser-vessel.ts:565,1206,1213,1324-1359,1443`; `shared-holder-core.ts:494-501`; `shared-holder.worker.ts:26-44,61`; `worker-handle.ts:39`; `main.ts:53-62,111-142,303,399,408`.

!!! K3. The clean-realm ceremony (B4, shape R)

As spec.md B4's recommendation, with the sharpened residuals of §2.2 and these build notes:
* `realmTainted` latch set at the first person's-plugin module evaluation (the census in M1 knows the moment); `custody:open` refuses `realm-tainted` from a tainted realm; lock and re-ask navigate (`location.reload()` under the unload hold); the mirror boots only after the worker answers `opened`.
* The ask page calls `navigator.credentials.get({publicKey:{rpId: location.hostname, extensions:{prf:{eval:{first: salt}}}}})` in the clean realm, posts the 32 bytes to the worker once, zeroes its buffer. The rpId is the vessel's served origin (§6 Q7). `get()` needs no gesture (row 2.5), but the house calls it from the person's tap anyway so the OS prompt reads as answered, not ambient.
* The plain-words rule stands beside every ask: //if your wiki shows, any ask is fake.//
* Where PRF reads absent (measured per device by `tools/capability-probe/`), the passphrase is the daily route under the same clean-realm rule.
* The bind of a passkey slot (`create()` with `prf`) runs top-level in the clean realm; Safari answers `enabled:false` on create for some providers (row 3), so the bind completes on the first `get()` that returns `results`.

''Tests'' as spec.md B4 (`ask-refuses-in-tainted-realm`, `lock-reloads-the-realm`, `prf-output-never-rests`, `passkey-slot-binds-and-opens` with the Chromium virtual authenticator). Add `ask-never-paints-over-a-wiki`: no `custody:open` ask element exists in a document where `data-lar-mirror` reads a width. ''Control:'' the clean realm paints the ask and no mirror.

!!! S. The seal: steps 2 and 3 for the browser store; the plugin gate opens (C1-C3)

Unchanged from spec.md C, with one re-cut: the blocker row C1e reads "''waits on W's cutover'' (`sealed-store.mem:356`; road `:732-736`)", not O1. Order: K2 → C1a, C1d → C1b → C1c → [W's session signer] → C2a → C2b, C2c → C2d, C2e → C3. The gate field `sealedRest` rides the `port:open` grant.

